<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|tmdoc>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|The <TeXmacs> developer's guide>

  This guide gathers the documentation written for the people who extend
  <TeXmacs> or work on it: how the program is put together, how a document
  is represented, how to program the editor in <scheme>, how to write style
  files and plug-ins, how to talk to other systems, and how fonts become
  glyphs. Several of these chapters are also reachable from the
  <hlink|manual|../main/man-manual.en.tm> and from the <hlink|reference
  guide|../main/man-reference.en.tm>; they are collected here so that the
  developer's material can be browsed on its own.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|About the source code of <TeXmacs>|source/source.en.tm>

    <branch|The <TeXmacs> document format|format/basics/basics.en.tm>

    <branch|The <scheme> extension language|scheme/scheme.en.tm>

    <branch|Writing style files and packages|style/style.en.tm>

    <branch|The plug-in system|plugin/plugins.en.tm>

    <branch|Interfacing <TeXmacs> with other programs|interface/interface.en.tm>

    <branch|Fonts, from selection to glyph|fonts/fonts.en.tm>
  </traverse>

